diff --git a/docs/COUNTED_MIPS_RELOCATIONS.md b/docs/COUNTED_MIPS_RELOCATIONS.md
index d0d4a85e..c479693c 100644
--- a/docs/COUNTED_MIPS_RELOCATIONS.md
+++ b/docs/COUNTED_MIPS_RELOCATIONS.md
@@ -73,3 +73,45 @@ python -m unittest discover -s tools/tests -p test_counted_mips_relocations.py
 python -m unittest discover -s tools/tests -p test_counted_relocation_discovery.py
 python -m unittest discover -s tools/tests -p test_aot_overlay_pipeline.py
 ```
+
+## Separate streams
+
+Some engines store each image and its stream as two members of an archive
+instead of one counted container. The stream format and the four relocation
+kinds are the same; only the layout differs. `parse_stream(image, stream)`
+reads one such pair: the stream must be whole words that end exactly at the
+`0xFFFFFFFF` terminator, every target must lie inside the image, and no target
+may repeat.
+
+```python
+from counted_mips_relocations import parse_stream, relocate
+
+member = parse_stream(image_bytes, stream_bytes)
+image = relocate(member, independently_verified_image_base)
+```
+
+The AOT pipeline accepts these pairs as `relocated_extent_members`:
+
+```json
+{"method": "relocated_extent_members",
+ "members": [{"name": "MODULE",
+              "image":       {"file": "DATA.ARC", "file_offset": "0x10", "size": "0x2000", "sha256": "..."},
+              "relocations": {"file": "DATA.ARC", "file_offset": "0x2010", "size": "0x90", "sha256": "..."},
+              "relocation_count": 33,
+              "placements": [{"load_addr": "0x80150000"}]}]}
+```
+
+The archive's own index (names, offsets, sizes) is not parsed by the core. A
+title's tooling reads it from the player's disc and writes the extents into
+the profile; the SHA-256 of each extent pins the bytes the pipeline relocates.
+As with counted containers there is no destination address in the data: every
+placement must be established from the original loader, and a newly
+encountered heap placement stays interpreted until its own variant is added.
+Member names must be unique; each placement becomes the source `NAME@ADDRESS`.
+
+The separate-stream reader was compared byte for byte with the owned USA Rev 1
+Spider-Man 2: Enter Electro relocation routine (`0x8001EEF0`), executed
+instruction by instruction, for 28 modules at six RAM bases each, including the
+heap placements a play session established: 168 complete-image comparisons
+passed. A placement four bytes off, and the unrelocated image, both failed the
+same comparison. Owned bytes and captures are not part of this repository.
